From ea40a58439ba0fe81db6ffe77dd4912cccede37e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahman Bazarov <96785952+JustRahman@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:25:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add temporal VAE tiling for LTX-Video decode

AutoencoderKLLTXVideo::decode() gets an overload which decodes the latent
video in overlapping chunks of latent frames and cross-fades the overlapping
video frames, so the peak memory of the decoder is bounded by the chunk
instead of the whole clip. The frame decoded from the first latent frame of
a chunk which doesn't start the video is dropped, because the previous chunk
has already produced it.

The option is off by default and is exposed as
VideoGenerationConfig::vae_tile_sample_min_num_frames /
vae_tile_sample_stride_num_frames (names follow diffusers) and as arguments
of AutoencoderKLLTXVideo.decode() in Python.
